ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-93, D-94): filters drawn only where they reach the visible area, large blurs at a reduced resolution
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: SVG filters cost as much as their whole region, linebender/resvg#790 and #1192)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg, linked to #1192 (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release draws filtered layers only within reach of the canvas, blurs large sigmas at a reduced resolution and reuses equal feTurbulence results, or this patch no longer applies

resvg drew every filtered group over its whole filter region, at the scale asked, however little of
it the canvas shows: a region of the canvas cost as much as the whole document, and a zoomed-in view
of a document with filters cost its whole area at that zoom. Here:
- a layer is drawn only within reach of the visible area (render::Context::visible): for a filtered
  group, the reach of its filters (filter::reach(): the box blur's exact width, offsets, morphology,
  displacement, convolution, lighting); a filter whose result may depend on its whole region
  (feTile, feImage, stitched feTurbulence) keeps its whole region, as before. Groups outside the
  reach are not drawn at all, nor are layers outside the visible area (tiny-skia 0.12 drew a one-row
  pixmap placed just above the canvas onto the canvas's first row);
- a primitive's subregion is cleared around within its result's pixels, wherever the subregion lies
  (it may now lie partly or wholly outside a layer drawn only in part);
- large blurs at a reduced resolution, as Skia blurs (D-94): a blur whose sigma passes 4 pixels is
  computed on a copy reduced about 2^n times on that axis (each reduced pixel the mean of the area
  it covers, edges on the region's), with a sigma of at most 4 there, and enlarged back with
  bilinear interpolation (filter::blur()); a lone such blur of the whole region, on a group with
  no clip path or mask, draws the group itself on the reduced layer, enlarged within the filter
  region at full resolution (filter::reduction(), render::render_reduced()). Against resvg's own
  references, in the tests with blurs, at most 19 levels on a few pixels and 1.5 on average (resvg
  and Chromium differ by 1.75 on the owner's artwork, D-90);
- a layer is laid over its parent directly when source-over (render::composite()): tiny-skia draws
  every pixmap through its high-precision pipeline, half the time of a document of large layers;
  its rounding differs by at most 3 levels;
- equal feTurbulence results (same noise over the same pixels) are computed once per render
  (filter::Cache, the four most recent): a document may use one noise in several filters.
Drawing within reach gives the pixels of the whole region, but for anti-aliased edges, whose coverage
may differ by a rounding step when a layer starts elsewhere (as between any two tiles). resvg's own
tests: 1,656 of 1,730 pass; the 74 others differ by the blurs, the rounding and those edges.

